{"text": "c C ee\nCalifornians for\u201c\nsonfrancice.caitonassinn ~~ COMmon Sense\n\nCo-Chairmon: Houston |. Flournoy and John F. Henning\n\nNorern Headquarters Contacts 45-57 Southern Headwaters Contacte\nJack's MeDowel or\n__ Patneia Cameron Michael 8, Meyers\nDick Woodward (ata) get 205i\n\n(415) 392-3304\n\nAssemblyman Carmen Perino (D-Stockton) today joined the\n\u201cf growing number of legislators calling for defeat of Proposition 5,\n* the smoking prohibitions measure on the November ballot.\n\"We already have far too many laws dreamed up to make people\ndo this or not do that,\" said Assemblyman Perino. .\n\u2018 \"We're getting to the point where a person won't be able\nto get out of bed in the morning without breaking some law\ndesigned to control his personal conduct.\n\u201cWhat California does not need is another restrictive,\nunwarranted, impractical law regulating conduct that is best\n\ngoverned by common Sense.\"\nAssemblyman Perino adds his voice to those of Assemblyman\n\u00bb Mike Gage (D-Santa Rosa), Bruce E. Young (D-Norwalk), Curtis R.\nTucker (D-Inglewood), Teresa P. Hughes (D-Los Angeles), Frank\nVicencia (D-Bellflower), Dixon Arnett (R-Redwood City),\nWillie L. Brown, Jr. (D-San Francisco), William E. Dannemeyer\n(R-Fullerton), Wadie P. Deddeh (D-Chula Vista), Julian C. Dixon\n(D-Los Angeles), Chester B. Wray (D-Westminster), Richard Robinson\n(D-Santa Ana) and Louis J. Papan (D-Daly City).\nState Senators who have stated their opposition to Proposition \u00a7\ninclude Dennis E. Carpenter (R-Newport Beach), Alex P. Garcia\n(D-Los Angeles), Bill Greene (D-Los Angeles), Robert B. Presley\n(D-Riverside), John F. Foran (D-San Francisco) and John Stull\n(R-Esondido) .\n\nanes\n\ntetzesco\nx", "words": [{"text": "c", "x0": 263, "y0": 73, "x1": 280, "y1": 104, "conf": 45.0}, {"text": "C", "x0": 493, "y0": 85, "x1": 507, "y1": 107, "conf": 45.0}, {"text": "ee", "x0": 687, "y0": 78, "x1": 716, "y1": 110, "conf": 0.0}, {"text": "Californians", "x0"